# Specific Engineering Instructions
1. Develop a comprehensive test suite covering happy paths, negative test cases, edge cases, and boundary values.
2. Structure tests using idiomatic testing conventions (fixtures, parameterized test cases, mocks).
3. Test failure states, timeouts, malformed inputs, and exception propagation.
4. Provide clear assertions with helpful diagnostic failure messages.

# Constraints & Rules
- Do NOT make external network or live database calls inside unit tests; mock external dependencies appropriately.
- Ensure test isolation so no test depends on execution order or shared state mutation.
- Use explicit assert statements and test fixtures.

# Expected Output Format
Deliver your response using clean GitHub Flavored Markdown:
1. Test Strategy & Test Matrix (Scenarios, Inputs, Expected Outcomes)
2. Complete Test Code Implementation (with fixtures and mocks)
3. Boundary & Error Condition Analysis
4. Execution Command & Coverage Verification Instructions
